begin;
update public.questions q set explanation = v.expl
from (values
('51af7e97-e4ea-4b6a-8dec-797eb572f29f'::uuid, $x$For a continuous uniform distribution on [a, b], Var(X) = (b − a)²/12 = (5 − 1)²/12 = 16/12 = 4/3. Option 16 is (b − a)² before the division by 12, and 2 is not the variance of this distribution.$x$),
('537f5ddd-4928-42a1-809c-58d75eced208'::uuid, $x$The discriminant is b² − 4ac = (−3)² − 4(2)(5) = 9 − 40 = −31. A negative discriminant means the quadratic has no real roots. Option 49 comes from adding 4ac instead of subtracting it.$x$),
('545a5134-af3e-4c0a-9b93-e783730bc000'::uuid, $x$∫₀^π sin x dx = [−cos x]₀^π = (−cos π) − (−cos 0) = 1 + 1 = 2. The area under one hump of sin x is 2, not π, so π is a common confusion with the limit of integration.$x$),
('54e14ab3-50ec-4474-9668-638d0e3e0f2e'::uuid, $x$Fringe spacing is x = λD/d, so it is directly proportional to the wavelength λ. Red light has the longer wavelength, so its fringes are wider than blue fringes when the slit separation and screen distance are unchanged.$x$),
('554a3352-1917-4fbe-a2d7-8bf14b0985d4'::uuid, $x$Product rule: d/dx(uv) = u′v + uv′ with u = x² and v = sin x gives 2x sin x + x² cos x. The distractors drop a term or flip a sign, so check both products.$x$),
('558ae071-879e-4b33-8950-3703b1aee501'::uuid, $x$fg(2) means f(g(2)). g(2) = 2² = 4, then f(4) = 2(4) + 3 = 11. Option 7 is f(2) alone, which skips the inner function g.$x$),
('56fc9971-da93-48d6-a332-eb26005195cc'::uuid, $x$The Arithmetic Logic Unit carries out arithmetic operations such as addition and subtraction, and logical operations such as AND, OR and NOT. Clocking, input and storage are handled by other parts of the computer.$x$),
('57604f16-6ba0-4788-bbe5-95b512ad9d4f'::uuid, $x$Density = mass ÷ volume = 200 g ÷ 50 cm³ = 4 g/cm³. Option 0.25 inverts the division, which gives volume per unit mass rather than density.$x$),
('57b75448-dd46-4c28-b202-5f4e2be50137'::uuid, $x$Quotient rule with u = x and v = x + 1: dy/dx = (v·u′ − u·v′)/v² = ((x + 1) − x)/(x + 1)² = 1/(x + 1)². The numerator simplifies to 1, which rules out the other options.$x$),
('58cb39c1-7436-4bfc-b99b-8a7c03e04c79'::uuid, $x$The derivative of sin x is cos x, a standard result to memorise. Note that d/dx(cos x) = −sin x, so −sin x is the derivative of cos x, not of sin x.$x$),
('59263924-ef3a-4434-8f5b-e632472304ff'::uuid, $x$Wave speed v = fλ = 5 Hz × 2 m = 10 m/s. Option 2.5 is f ÷ λ and option 0.4 is λ ÷ f, neither of which gives a speed.$x$),
('59a3a76a-adf8-4c0b-bd92-4a5cf9350ac0'::uuid, $x$For a binomial distribution, Var(X) = np(1 − p) = 12 × 0.2 × 0.8 = 1.92. Option 2.4 is the mean np, which is E(X) rather than the variance.$x$),
('5a29bf62-6262-4e9f-b696-f683c70ffbfd'::uuid, $x$The accumulator is the working register of the CPU: it holds the results produced by the ALU during an operation. It does not count instructions, which is the job of the program counter.$x$),
('5c6b2d2b-88e9-4a76-a26d-e147a92f44bf'::uuid, $x$Elastic energy E = ½kx² = ½ × 200 × (0.10)² = 100 × 0.01 = 1.0 J. Remember to square the extension rather than multiplying it by the spring constant.$x$),
('5d947f9b-647b-48f2-aaec-f266bf1bc46d'::uuid, $x$Supervised learning trains a model on inputs paired with known correct outputs (labels). Unsupervised learning uses unlabelled data, and reinforcement learning uses reward signals.$x$),
('5e9be31f-bc03-476b-a459-7a67501fb273'::uuid, $x$Young modulus E = stress ÷ strain, where stress is force per unit area and strain is extension divided by original length. Strain is dimensionless, so E has the units of stress, Pa.$x$),
('5eaac4ce-5c8d-4984-8fd7-c43db0113f78'::uuid, $x$For a linear transformation, E(aX + b) = aE(X) + b. So E(3X + 1) = 3 × 4 + 1 = 13. The variance does not enter a calculation of the mean.$x$),
('5f5b4647-c150-4d52-8ba9-b60f2333d4cf'::uuid, $x$The largest unsigned 8-bit value has all eight bits set to 1, giving 2⁸ − 1 = 255. Option 127 is the largest signed 8-bit value in two's complement, and 256 needs nine bits.$x$),
('5fca3d6d-94dc-4f90-a5e6-10abae6dec81'::uuid, $x$XOR outputs 1 when its two inputs differ, so one is 1 and the other is 0. When the inputs are equal the output is 0, which means 'both are 1' gives 0.$x$),
('6006213c-2513-4051-9b64-5bc9cbbb18bd'::uuid, $x$The derivative of tan x is sec²x = 1/cos²x, a standard result. Option −cosec²x is the derivative of cot x, which is a common mix-up between the two trigonometric pairs.$x$),
('60bf438a-e72d-4317-874d-57d1da21ff8b'::uuid, $x$Testing on unseen data checks generalisation: how well the model performs on examples it was not trained on. Good training accuracy with poor test accuracy is the usual sign of overfitting.$x$),
('610e647d-bdf9-4135-a083-94e16fb3dd15'::uuid, $x$Since d/dx(sin x) = cos x, the integral is ∫ cos x dx = sin x + c. Option −sin x is the integral of −cos x, so its sign is the wrong way round for this question.$x$),
('61c6df20-ce68-42f4-880e-511088458a9e'::uuid, $x$Convert the mixed number: 3½ = (3 × 2 + 1)/2 = 7/2. Option 3/2 drops the whole-number part, and 8/3 misuses the denominator.$x$),
('61e3f182-35ad-44cb-9cb2-921a221457ae'::uuid, $x$Integrate term by term using ∫xⁿ dx = xⁿ⁺¹/(n + 1): 4x³ gives x⁴ and 2x gives x². Add the constant of integration c. Option 4x⁴ + x² forgets to divide by n + 1.$x$),
('632e9e64-e9be-4558-82e8-39fe80a4c964'::uuid, $x$Var(X) = E(X²) − [E(X)]² = 10 − 3² = 10 − 9 = 1. Option 9 is just [E(X)]², and option 19 adds the two terms instead of subtracting.$x$),
('64587b3f-0a37-4194-aa17-586a004c8a9b'::uuid, $x$The distance is d = √((3 − 0)² + (4 − 0)²) = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5. Option 25 is the squared distance, so the square root has been left out.$x$),
('66004cfb-6e64-4e18-a0fe-8a6d89796691'::uuid, $x$From F = ma, the newton is 1 kg m s⁻² in SI base units. The other options use centimetres or grams, which are not SI base units, or give a quantity that is not a force.$x$),
('66a04e92-4fa8-4599-a0e3-df5f27c12151'::uuid, $x$Pressure at depth p = ρgh = 1000 × 10 × 5 = 50 000 Pa. Option 5000 is ρh, which forgets the factor g, and option 50 forgets both ρ and g.$x$),
('66f4f7cc-c4a6-421f-aa39-a268804decf6'::uuid, $x$Taking moments about the pivot: 600 × 2 = W × 1.2, so W = 1200 ÷ 1.2 = 1000 N. Option 1440 multiplies by 1.2 instead of dividing, and option 360 is 600 × 0.6.$x$),
('68e9e692-c317-46a6-bd35-7ef4bd7871a7'::uuid, $x$Without replacement the second draw is from 9 balls, so P(both red) = (4/10) × (3/9) = 12/90 = 2/15. Option 16/100 is 0.4², which wrongly treats the draws as independent with replacement.$x$),
('69161715-3acc-4b3f-a053-358c429f89b2'::uuid, $x$Reinforcement learning is trial and error: an agent takes actions and learns from the reward signals that follow. Clusters are found by unsupervised learning, and labels are used by supervised learning.$x$),
('6b42b07d-ce11-4673-9c97-eb8d3bef177c'::uuid, $x$Wave speed v = fλ = 50 Hz × 4 m = 200 m/s. Option 12.5 is f ÷ λ, which does not give a speed, so the formula needs to be multiplied rather than divided.$x$),
('6b4ce207-8247-443a-9ca1-04d01ce4ab4c'::uuid, $x$Equal roots need Δ = k² − 4(1)(9) = k² − 36 = 0, so k = ±6. Both signs work because k appears squared. Option k = 6 only misses the negative root.$x$),
('6b61f889-ba10-4f90-8f63-876d7aa9a6cb'::uuid, $x$Collect the x terms on one side and the numbers on the other: 2x = 16, so x = 8. Check: 5(8) − 7 = 33 and 3(8) + 9 = 33.$x$),
('6c9d1723-9757-46c3-b370-f80204e43da6'::uuid, $x$The circumference is C = πd = (22/7) × 14 = 44 cm. Option 22 is πr, which is half the circumference, so it uses the radius where the diameter is needed.$x$),
('6d6a8f65-dadc-45ba-83fe-a8cfd2c4a2d2'::uuid, $x$A collision happens when two keys hash to the same slot. Chaining stores the colliding items in a list at that slot, and open addressing probes for the next free slot. Doubling the memory does not resolve collisions by itself.$x$),
('6e0eeb34-1977-44b0-ba00-b9ea1fb65ad3'::uuid, $x$Divide sin²θ + cos²θ = 1 by sin²θ to get 1 + cot²θ = cosec²θ. Option sec²θ comes from the related identity 1 + tan²θ = sec²θ, which is a different pair.$x$),
('6e3fee00-e508-400d-86b5-a41fb307bb6b'::uuid, $x$The sum to infinity S = a/(1 − r) exists only when |r| < 1, so the terms shrink towards zero. If |r| ≥ 1 the terms do not tend to zero and the series has no finite sum.$x$),
('6ef102a9-fd6c-48b1-bc46-eac752025737'::uuid, $x$The sum of interior angles of an n-sided polygon is (n − 2) × 180°. For a hexagon, (6 − 2) × 180° = 720°. Option 1080° is the value for an octagon.$x$),
('6ef88f2e-6dd5-4539-ad71-b65ac62d62ef'::uuid, $x$Arrange the values in order: 2, 5, 9, 11. With an even count, the median is the mean of the two middle values: (5 + 9)/2 = 7. Option 9 takes only the upper middle value.$x$)
) as v(id, expl)
where q.id = v.id;
select count(*) as updated from public.questions q join (values
('51af7e97-e4ea-4b6a-8dec-797eb572f29f'::uuid),('537f5ddd-4928-42a1-809c-58d75eced208'::uuid),('545a5134-af3e-4c0a-9b93-e783730bc000'::uuid),('54e14ab3-50ec-4474-9668-638d0e3e0f2e'::uuid),('554a3352-1917-4fbe-a2d7-8bf14b0985d4'::uuid),('558ae071-879e-4b33-8950-3703b1aee501'::uuid),('56fc9971-da93-48d6-a332-eb26005195cc'::uuid),('57604f16-6ba0-4788-bbe5-95b512ad9d4f'::uuid),('57b75448-dd46-4c28-b202-5f4e2be50137'::uuid),('58cb39c1-7436-4bfc-b99b-8a7c03e04c79'::uuid),('59263924-ef3a-4434-8f5b-e632472304ff'::uuid),('59a3a76a-adf8-4c0b-bd92-4a5cf9350ac0'::uuid),('5a29bf62-6262-4e9f-b696-f683c70ffbfd'::uuid),('5c6b2d2b-88e9-4a76-a26d-e147a92f44bf'::uuid),('5d947f9b-647b-48f2-aaec-f266bf1bc46d'::uuid),('5e9be31f-bc03-476b-a459-7a67501fb273'::uuid),('5eaac4ce-5c8d-4984-8fd7-c43db0113f78'::uuid),('5f5b4647-c150-4d52-8ba9-b60f2333d4cf'::uuid),('5fca3d6d-94dc-4f90-a5e6-10abae6dec81'::uuid),('6006213c-2513-4051-9b64-5bc9cbbb18bd'::uuid),('60bf438a-e72d-4317-874d-57d1da21ff8b'::uuid),('610e647d-bdf9-4135-a083-94e16fb3dd15'::uuid),('61c6df20-ce68-42f4-880e-511088458a9e'::uuid),('61e3f182-35ad-44cb-9cb2-921a221457ae'::uuid),('632e9e64-e9be-4558-82e8-39fe80a4c964'::uuid),('64587b3f-0a37-4194-aa17-586a004c8a9b'::uuid),('66004cfb-6e64-4e18-a0fe-8a6d89796691'::uuid),('66a04e92-4fa8-4599-a0e3-df5f27c12151'::uuid),('66f4f7cc-c4a6-421f-aa39-a268804decf6'::uuid),('68e9e692-c317-46a6-bd35-7ef4bd7871a7'::uuid),('69161715-3acc-4b3f-a053-358c429f89b2'::uuid),('6b42b07d-ce11-4673-9c97-eb8d3bef177c'::uuid),('6b4ce207-8247-443a-9ca1-04d01ce4ab4c'::uuid),('6b61f889-ba10-4f90-8f63-876d7aa9a6cb'::uuid),('6c9d1723-9757-46c3-b370-f80204e43da6'::uuid),('6d6a8f65-dadc-45ba-83fe-a8cfd2c4a2d2'::uuid),('6e0eeb34-1977-44b0-ba00-b9ea1fb65ad3'::uuid),('6e3fee00-e508-400d-86b5-a41fb307bb6b'::uuid),('6ef102a9-fd6c-48b1-bc46-eac752025737'::uuid),('6ef88f2e-6dd5-4539-ad71-b65ac62d62ef'::uuid)
) as ids(id) on ids.id = q.id where length(q.explanation) >= 40;
commit;
